cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "authgent: open-source reference implementation of the IETF agent-identity stack"
message: "If you reference authgent in research, an IETF Implementation Status section, or a published article, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Agnihotri
    given-names: Dhruv
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/authgent/authgent"
url: "https://github.com/authgent/authgent"
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: "draft-agnihotri-oauth-agent-impl-status-00"
    description: "IETF Internet-Draft documenting authgent as the reference implementation of draft-ietf-oauth-identity-chaining-14 and draft-ietf-oauth-transaction-tokens-08, posted 2026-06-12."
  - type: url
    value: "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-agnihotri-oauth-agent-impl-status/"
    description: "IETF Datatracker page for the Implementation Status I-D."
abstract: >
  authgent is a self-hosted OAuth 2.1 authorization server for AI agents.
  It is the open-source reference implementation of
  draft-ietf-oauth-identity-chaining-15 (cross-domain delegation) and
  draft-ietf-oauth-transaction-tokens-08 (intra-domain transaction
  context propagation), in addition to RFC 8693 nested-act delegation
  chains, RFC 9449 DPoP, RFC 9728 Protected Resource Metadata, RFC 7591
  Dynamic Client Registration, and the MCP 2026-07-28 authorization
  spec. Apache 2.0.
keywords:
  - oauth
  - oauth2.1
  - identity-chaining
  - transaction-tokens
  - rfc-8693
  - rfc-9449
  - dpop
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - agent-authentication
  - delegation
  - ietf
preferred-citation:
  type: software
  title: "authgent — IETF agent-identity reference implementation"
  authors:
    - family-names: Agnihotri
      given-names: Dhruv
  year: 2026
  url: "https://github.com/authgent/authgent"
